            <p class="- topic/p ">You want to add 2 from 3 . The equation will look like 3+2=5. You enter 3 , press + ,
                enter 2, press equlas</p>
            <p class="- topic/p ">The result 5 displays on screen</p>
        </example>
    </taskbody>
</task></topic><topic xmlns:ot-placeholder="http://suite-sol.com/namespaces/ot-placeholder" break-before="true" is-chapter="true" class="+ topic/topic pdf2-d/placeholder " id="d98e38" topicrefclass="+ map/topicref mapgroup-d/topichead "><title class="- topic/title "><ph class="- topic/ph topic/title-wrapper ">subtract</ph></title><concept class="- topic/topic concept/concept " id="unique_3" topicrefclass="- map/topicref " nd:nd-id="what_is_subtract_of_numbers" oid="what_is_subtract_of_numbers" specializations="@props/deliveryTarget">
    <title class="- topic/title "><ph class="- topic/ph topic/title-wrapper ">What is subtract of numbers</ph></title>
    <shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">Here you will learn what is subtraction</shortdesc>
    <conbody class="- topic/body  concept/conbody ">
        <p class="- topic/p ">Subtraction is the process of finding the <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">difference between two numbers</b> by taking
            one number away from another. </p>
        <p class="- topic/p ">When using a calculator, you <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">enter the first number</b>, <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">press the minus (–)</b>
            button, <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">enter the second number</b>, <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">then press equals (=)</b> to get the
            result.</p>
        <p class="- topic/p "> It shows how much remains after removing one value from another.</p>
    </conbody>
</concept><task class="- topic/topic task/task " id="unique_4" topicrefclass="- map/topicref " nd:nd-id="how_to_subtract_numbers" oid="how_to_subtract_numbers" specializations="@props/deliveryTarget">
